{"builder":"Goal: one pull request that adds a --shout flag to greet-cli and meets every line of issue.expect.\n\nContext: bin/greet.js takes the first argument that does not start with `--` as the name and prints `${greeting(name)}\\n`, where src/greet.js exports `greeting = (name) => `Hello, ${name}!``. Tests are in test/greet.test.js and run with `npm test` (node --test). .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes the docs/ directory to GitHub Pages on push to main, so docs/index.md is the source of the published page.\n\nSteps:\n1. In bin/greet.js, detect `--shout` among process.argv.slice(2) (in any position relative to the name). When present, print the greeting in upper case, e.g. `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline. Keep name parsing as it is, so `--shout` is never taken as the name. You may add a helper in src/greet.js (e.g. a shout option or function), but do not change what `greeting(name)` returns.\n2. Without --shout, the output must stay exactly as today: `node bin/greet.js Ada` prints `Hello, Ada!\\n`; with no name it still writes `usage: greet <name>` to stderr and exits 2. You may mention --shout in the usage text only if the no-name behaviour (stderr, exit code 2) is otherwise unchanged; simplest is to leave it alone.\n3. Update docs/index.md to document --shout: show the usage `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>` and state that it prints the greeting in upper case (e.g. `HELLO, <NAME>!`). Keep it in docs/index.md so the existing pages workflow publishes it; do not change .github/workflows/pages.yml.\n4. Add tests to test/greet.test.js: one that runs `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` and expects `HELLO, ADA!\\n`, and keep the existing tests that check unchanged output without the flag.\n5. Run `npm test` and confirm all tests pass, then open the pull request. In the PR description, note that the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ will only list --shout after merge, when the pages workflow deploys docs/.","verifier":"Run every check at the pull request's head, from the repository root. Run `npm install` first only if package.json at the head added dependencies.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` and `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout`, and also `node bin/greet.js Ada` to get the normal greeting.\nPASS: each --shout run exits 0 and its stdout equals the upper-case form of the normal greeting for the same name (for the current greeting, `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline).\nFAIL: either --shout run exits non-zero, prints the usage message, prints the greeting not in upper case, or prints something other than the upper-cased greeting.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun: at the head, `node bin/greet.js Ada; echo \"exit=$?\"` and `node bin/greet.js; echo \"exit=$?\"` (capture stdout and stderr separately). Then get the same outputs from the code before the change (e.g. `git stash`-free: `git worktree add /tmp/greet-base <merge-base of the PR>` or `git show <merge-base>:bin/greet.js` with its src) and compare. Also run `npm test` at the head.\nPASS: `node bin/greet.js Ada` prints exactly `Hello, Ada!\\n` with exit 0, the no-name run behaves the same as before the change (stdout, stderr and exit code 2 match the base), and `npm test` passes.\nFAIL: any output or exit code differs from the base when --shout is not given, or `npm test` fails.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRead: docs/index.md at the head.\nPASS: the file mentions `--shout` and says what it does (prints the greeting in upper case).\nFAIL: docs/index.md does not mention --shout, or mentions it without saying what it does.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nThe live page can only be seen after merge; do not fetch it. Check what the head contains that will produce it. Read: .github/workflows/pages.yml and docs/index.md at the head.\nPASS: .github/workflows/pages.yml still runs on push to main and uploads the `docs` directory as the Pages artifact and deploys it, and docs/index.md at the head lists --shout (so the published page will list it once merged).\nFAIL: the workflow no longer publishes docs/ on push to main (removed, path changed, trigger changed), or docs/index.md at the head does not list --shout.\n\nAdvisory\n- Check test/greet.test.js has a test for the --shout output; its absence is worth noting but is not a FAIL.\n- Note whether --shout works when placed before and after the name; both are covered in Check 1.\n- Note any change to what `greeting(name)` in src/greet.js returns."}